Typed QueryIntent handoff:
{"intent":{"acceptance_tests":["Returns exactly 5 rows; owner_ids are in ascending order; all returned owner_ids are distinct and valid"],"aggregation":["COUNT(*)"],"assumptions":["Account numbers are unique; owner_id is a numeric or sortable field; each account has exactly one owner"],"entities":["Account","Owner"],"expected_shape":["5 rows with columns: owner_id"],"ordering":["Owner.owner_id ASC"],"predicates":["Account.account_number = '108'"],"relationships":["Account-[:SENT_TO]->Account","Account-[:OWNED_BY]->Owner"],"uncertainties":["Whether account 108 exists; whether it has sent money to any accounts; whether those accounts have owners"]},"question":"Who owns the accounts that account number 108 has sent money to? Give the five lowest owner ids in ascending order."}

How many distinct ordered pairs of two *different* accounts owned by the same party have a direct transfer running from the first to the second? Count each pair once however many transfers run between them.

